1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,125
[tense music]

2
00:00:04,458 --> 00:00:07,167
All those scrolls you had
Lloyd running around with,

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:09,250
is this what you
were researching?

4
00:00:09,917 --> 00:00:12,167
Not sure I can pull it off.

5
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:16,000
It's arriving too soon.
Too soon!

6
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:17,208
What are you saying?

7
00:00:17,292 --> 00:00:18,667
Raccoon? Baboon?

8
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:20,333
-[crate clatters]
-[Master Wu yelps]

9
00:00:22,042 --> 00:00:24,750
[gasps] Only unity can save us.

10
00:00:25,375 --> 00:00:27,833
Separate, we have no chance.

11
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:30,125
[thunder crashing]

12
00:00:30,208 --> 00:00:33,083
[knocking]

13
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:35,583
Ugh, do you know
what time it is?

14
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:38,667
Trying to get my beauty
sleep here. Boss!

15
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:40,750
Bunch of jerks that apparently
don't care about my beauty

16
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:41,958
are here to see you.

17
00:00:44,042 --> 00:00:46,625
-We've come for Jay.
-Whatever you've done to him--

18
00:00:46,708 --> 00:00:51,292
Me? The Merge left
Jay Walker without his memory.

19
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:55,000
Lost, alone, friendless.

20
00:00:55,083 --> 00:00:59,917
I found him. Helped him
when no one else did.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,667
Where were you?

22
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:04,417
He's one of us, Ras.
Let him out.

23
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,750
Too late. He's gone.

24
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:10,625
Jay was here for one
purpose, to win matches.

25
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,000
He failed that purpose,
so I sent him away.

26
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:18,917
[chain clacking]

27
00:01:19,875 --> 00:01:25,125
If you truly value Jay, leave
the games and go after him.

28
00:01:27,792 --> 00:01:30,042
-Come on, we need to...
-[Riyu rumbles]

29
00:01:30,125 --> 00:01:33,625
What? Maybe we can catch
up to Jay before daylight.

30
00:01:33,708 --> 00:01:36,625
Nya, Ras is playing us.

31
00:01:36,708 --> 00:01:39,708
He sent Jay away because he
wants us to go after him.

32
00:01:39,792 --> 00:01:41,750
Which we will. Right?

33
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:43,042
Jay needs us.

34
00:01:43,125 --> 00:01:44,792
Not only has he
lost his memories,

35
00:01:44,875 --> 00:01:46,667
he used the Gong of Shattering!

36
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:49,250
We have to find a way to
heal his inner goodness!

37
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:51,708
We have to save him!

38
00:01:51,792 --> 00:01:53,667
We do, but this tournament

39
00:01:53,750 --> 00:01:55,792
is a threat to
the Source Dragons,

40
00:01:55,875 --> 00:01:57,958
to the Merged Lands themselves.

41
00:01:58,042 --> 00:02:02,375
If our world is destroyed,
there will be no Jay to save.

42
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:05,458
Before everything changed,
Master Wu told me,

43
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:07,583
"Only unity can save us."

44
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:09,833
Without Jay, we aren't united.

45
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:14,042
When the games are over,
when the world is saved,

46
00:02:14,125 --> 00:02:16,792
we'll find Jay.
I promise.

47
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:20,875
-[tender music]
-[footsteps clicking]

48
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:23,583
-What's wrong?
-During their fight,

49
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:26,375
Jay told Nya he worked
at the Administration.

50
00:02:26,458 --> 00:02:29,708
Wait, Jay is Agent Walker?

51
00:02:29,792 --> 00:02:32,167
Yeah, the only
person who might know

52
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,833
what happened to my parents.

53
00:02:33,917 --> 00:02:36,542
Great. So when this is all
over, we'll go find him.

54
00:02:36,625 --> 00:02:38,750
Then we can find your parents!

55
00:02:38,833 --> 00:02:41,083
But when will this all be over?

56
00:02:41,875 --> 00:02:44,583
Lloyd promised we'd
find my parents before.

57
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:47,167
Now he promised
Nya we'd find Jay.

58
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,583
But something always
gets in the way.

59
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,667
♪ Lost in the unknown,
so much to see ♪

60
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:56,750
♪ Together we will rise ♪

61
00:02:56,833 --> 00:02:59,917
♪ We fight ♪

62
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,208
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

63
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:05,875
[flame roaring]

64
00:03:06,542 --> 00:03:09,542
-[metal creaking]
-[Nya grunting]

65
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:18,500
Nya's training technique

66
00:03:18,583 --> 00:03:20,792
appears more
aggressive than usual.

67
00:03:20,875 --> 00:03:23,292
-[Nya yelling and screaming]
-[wood cracking]

68
00:03:24,417 --> 00:03:27,625
You mean angrier?
I can't blame her.

69
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,583
She's working
through some stuff.

70
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:31,542
She asked to be left alone.

71
00:03:31,625 --> 00:03:33,667
[Zane] But the games
will resume shortly.

72
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:36,875
She'll be there when we
need her. She always is.

73
00:03:36,958 --> 00:03:39,458
-[Nya yelling]
-[fists thumping]

74
00:03:39,542 --> 00:03:43,833
Poison, Shade, and, what
does this guy have again?

75
00:03:44,458 --> 00:03:47,625
Elemental power of looking mean?

76
00:03:47,708 --> 00:03:49,667
Ugh! This is impossible!

77
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:53,417
There's too many! [groans]]

78
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:56,583
Sora, studying your
opponents is good prep,

79
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:58,708
but you gotta find calm.

80
00:03:58,792 --> 00:04:01,583
Master Wu once said,
"The garden of confidence

81
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:06,000
grows in the soil of calm,
not the rocks of panic."

82
00:04:06,083 --> 00:04:09,417
My confidence isn't a garden.
It isn't even a shrub.

83
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,750
I'm pretty much
all rocks of panic.

84
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:14,500
What if I'm up against
Cinder or Nokt?

85
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,375
They can do Shatterspin!
I can't even do Spinjitzu!

86
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:22,000
These games are often
not about strength,

87
00:04:22,083 --> 00:04:24,625
but about out-maneuvering
your opponent.

88
00:04:24,708 --> 00:04:27,958
Zane's right. And Spinjitzu
is within your reach.

89
00:04:28,042 --> 00:04:29,500
You've got the
fundamentals down.

90
00:04:29,917 --> 00:04:33,292
Look, I know the games
are getting more intense

91
00:04:33,375 --> 00:04:35,250
and it's affecting all of us.

92
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:39,125
But remember, we're here for
more than just this competition.

93
00:04:39,208 --> 00:04:40,792
The mystery of the
Matriarch's death

94
00:04:40,875 --> 00:04:43,458
is somehow connected
to the games.

95
00:04:43,542 --> 00:04:45,667
And Ras wants to win badly,

96
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:48,958
so our job is to
make sure he doesn't.

97
00:04:49,042 --> 00:04:53,083
Even if it means winning
ourselves. We can do this.

98
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:55,958
And he doesn't think
he's a good leader.

99
00:04:56,625 --> 00:04:59,792
[Kai] Riyu? Can you hear me?

100
00:05:01,625 --> 00:05:02,667
[Riyu grumbles]

101
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:04,042
Riyu, don't give up.

102
00:05:04,125 --> 00:05:05,458
We have to tell you something

103
00:05:05,542 --> 00:05:07,125
before the other
three come back.

104
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:12,792
[fireworks exploding]

105
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:18,500
Are you ready?
I think you're. Yeah!

106
00:05:18,958 --> 00:05:22,042
When they talk about the
Tournament of the Sources,

107
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:26,375
they often say
"Legendary" and "Mythic."

108
00:05:26,458 --> 00:05:31,583
But now they'll also say
"Mega-tight" and "Stang-zoot"

109
00:05:31,667 --> 00:05:33,292
a new word I just made up.

110
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:35,667
Let the games continue!

111
00:05:36,125 --> 00:05:37,708
Get your umbrella hats on

112
00:05:37,792 --> 00:05:40,875
'cause it's about to
rain elemental powers!

113
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:45,625
First up today, it's the ninja
with cat ears and no fears.

114
00:05:45,708 --> 00:05:49,250
Sora, Elemental
Master of Technology!

115
00:05:49,333 --> 00:05:50,583
[crowd whooping and cheering]

116
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:52,833
-All right, Sora.
-You can do this.

117
00:05:52,917 --> 00:05:56,667
Versus the liquid warrior
who will never bore ya'.

118
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,125
From the Azure Reef,

119
00:05:58,208 --> 00:06:01,542
it's Kizzy, Elemental
Master of Balance!

120
00:06:01,625 --> 00:06:03,750
-You can do this.
-You got this, Sora.

121
00:06:03,833 --> 00:06:06,375
[crowd cheering]

122
00:06:06,458 --> 00:06:08,875
Okay, maybe I can do this.

123
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:10,375
These two masters

124
00:06:10,458 --> 00:06:14,250
will face the high-wire
obstacle extravaganza.

125
00:06:16,792 --> 00:06:18,958
The first to beat their
opponent to the finish line

126
00:06:19,042 --> 00:06:21,875
and kick the kettle drum wins.

127
00:06:21,958 --> 00:06:24,458
Stang-zoot, am I right?

128
00:06:24,542 --> 00:06:27,625
[spirited upbeat music]

129
00:06:29,875 --> 00:06:32,250
-[bell clangs]
-Go, go, go, go!

130
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:33,333
[Sora yelps]

131
00:06:33,417 --> 00:06:34,750
[tense music]

132
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:38,167
-[Kizzy whirring]
-[crowd applauds]

133
00:06:39,958 --> 00:06:41,292
[Sora] Whoa.

134
00:06:41,917 --> 00:06:45,125
Sora's competing against the
Elemental Master of Balance

135
00:06:45,208 --> 00:06:46,750
on a tightrope.

136
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:48,125
How is this even fair?

137
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:49,583
Have some faith in her.

138
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:51,500
Let's hope she has
faith in herself.

139
00:06:51,583 --> 00:06:53,375
[metallic clanging]

140
00:06:53,458 --> 00:06:56,292
[Sora] If Kizzy can use her
elemental power, so can I!

141
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,375
[Roby] What's this?
Our Elemental Master of Tech

142
00:06:59,458 --> 00:07:01,667
is turning her
obstacle into a tool!

143
00:07:02,542 --> 00:07:03,875
"Noice!"

144
00:07:03,958 --> 00:07:06,750
[Sora screams, groans]

145
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:11,750
-[flames hissing]
-[Kizzy whirring]

146
00:07:15,917 --> 00:07:18,333
[Roby] Whoa, Kizzy's showing
the fighting spirit

147
00:07:18,417 --> 00:07:19,750
that makes the
Reefling Water-Tides

148
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:21,917
the Lords of Coral Corral!

149
00:07:23,208 --> 00:07:25,542
[weapon whirring]

150
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,333
[flames booming]

151
00:07:29,417 --> 00:07:31,833
[Sora groans]

152
00:07:31,917 --> 00:07:34,750
Sorry, can't hang.
Got a drum to kick!

153
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:42,500
Just like Rontu taught me.
Jump, spin-kick, and through!

154
00:07:43,917 --> 00:07:48,375
-[Sora groans]
-[flames booming]

155
00:07:48,458 --> 00:07:49,917
[jubilant music]

156
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,958
We have a winner.

157
00:07:52,042 --> 00:07:54,667
[crowd cheering]

158
00:08:00,792 --> 00:08:02,208
No hard feelings, Kiz?

159
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,917
Master Kizzy, transfer time.

160
00:08:07,375 --> 00:08:10,292
[powers crackling]

161
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:15,625
Sora, you are now the
Elemental Master of Technology

162
00:08:15,708 --> 00:08:17,333
and Balance.

163
00:08:17,417 --> 00:08:21,583
Up next, she's smoking hot
and likes to fight a lot.

164
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:25,333
It's Wyldfyre, Elemental
Master of Heat!

165
00:08:25,417 --> 00:08:26,875
Oh, yeah.

166
00:08:26,958 --> 00:08:31,125
Versus the cloudy man
with the smoky hands!

167
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:34,917
Cinder, Elemental
Master of, poof, Smoke.

168
00:08:36,125 --> 00:08:40,750
Yes, finally! Payback time!

169
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:44,583
[Roby] Whoo, a classic.
Capture the flag!

170
00:08:44,667 --> 00:08:48,958
First to get it out
of the circle wins!

171
00:08:49,042 --> 00:08:52,917
Wyldfyre, I know you're itching
to take revenge for Kai,

172
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,125
but we got bigger
things to focus on.

173
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,750
Just go for the flag
and win the game.

174
00:08:57,833 --> 00:09:00,708
Don't worry, coach.
I'll cream him.

175
00:09:04,083 --> 00:09:06,917
[bell clangs]

176
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,792
-[flames hissing]
-[tense music]

177
00:09:12,708 --> 00:09:15,167
Wyldfyre, just grab the flag
before it's too late

178
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,583
-and they use the...
-[gong clangs]

179
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:20,125
-Oh, no.
-Oh, yeah.

180
00:09:22,875 --> 00:09:25,250
[Cinder booms]

181
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:29,583
-[Wyldfyre yelps]
-[crowd clapping]

182
00:09:29,667 --> 00:09:31,583
[Wyldfyre groans]

183
00:09:31,667 --> 00:09:34,000
[Cinder whirs and booms]

184
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,292
[tense music continues]

185
00:09:41,583 --> 00:09:45,542
-[crowd gasps]
-C'mon on, Wyldfyre. Get up!

186
00:09:45,625 --> 00:09:48,333
-[Cinder booms]
-[Wyldfyre yelps]

187
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:49,792
[all gasping]

188
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:54,958
-[crowd cheering]
-We have a winner. Whoop!

189
00:09:56,417 --> 00:09:59,292
[gasps] What happened?

190
00:09:59,375 --> 00:10:00,708
Are you okay?

191
00:10:01,333 --> 00:10:04,458
I'm totally stang-zoot.

192
00:10:04,542 --> 00:10:07,542
That curtain of fire was
amazing, BT-dub.

193
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:10,583
Sorry, but I have to
transfer your powers now.

194
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:17,208
-[Wyldfyre sighs]
-[powers crackling]

195
00:10:17,667 --> 00:10:20,250
[crowd cheering]

196
00:10:22,792 --> 00:10:26,583
-[powers crackling]
-[jubilant music]

197
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,583
[scoffs] They shouldn't
even be allowed

198
00:10:33,667 --> 00:10:36,542
to use the Gong of Shattering.
It's not fair.

199
00:10:36,625 --> 00:10:39,333
I thought the same
thing after Jay used it,

200
00:10:39,417 --> 00:10:41,125
but in combing
through the rules,

201
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:43,250
I found there is
technically no prohibition

202
00:10:43,333 --> 00:10:44,917
on the use of such items.

203
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,875
Which Ras must have known.

204
00:10:47,458 --> 00:10:50,000
[sniffs] Do you guys smell that?

205
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:53,000
[sniffs] It's not me, right?
I never know when it's me.

206
00:10:53,083 --> 00:10:55,875
[wind whooshing]

207
00:10:55,958 --> 00:10:58,917
The loser and her loser friends.

208
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,583
What do you want, Cinder?

209
00:11:00,667 --> 00:11:02,000
Hey, if it helps,

210
00:11:02,083 --> 00:11:03,875
you never stood
a chance in there, kid.

211
00:11:03,958 --> 00:11:05,667
Your mentor was Kai.

212
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,917
Get taught by a loser, all you
learn is how is lose, right?

213
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,083
[Wyldfyre yells]

214
00:11:11,958 --> 00:11:16,250
[laughs] You seriously just
tried to blast your power?

215
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:17,750
You forgot already?

216
00:11:18,833 --> 00:11:22,000
Bet I already know how to use
this power better than you.

217
00:11:22,375 --> 00:11:24,583
[fireball booms]

218
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,500
[security bots chittering]

219
00:11:28,583 --> 00:11:32,042
Dragons don't need
fire to fight. [groans]

220
00:11:32,125 --> 00:11:34,500
[Cinder yelps]

221
00:11:34,583 --> 00:11:38,292
-What the...?
-[Cinder yelping and groaning]

222
00:11:38,375 --> 00:11:41,375
[hover plate whirring]

223
00:11:42,292 --> 00:11:47,292
[groans] Please don't hurt me.

224
00:11:47,375 --> 00:11:49,250
I just wanted to
say congratulations.

225
00:11:53,042 --> 00:11:55,958
Please, please! Mercy!

226
00:11:56,042 --> 00:11:58,833
Such behavior defies logic.

227
00:12:00,625 --> 00:12:02,667
Break up those rabble-rousers.

228
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:10,625
Ninja, ganging up on the victor
that defeated your teammate.

229
00:12:10,708 --> 00:12:13,375
We haven't seen such
unsportsmanlike behavior

230
00:12:13,458 --> 00:12:14,750
in generations.

231
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:16,292
No, you've got it all wrong.

232
00:12:18,208 --> 00:12:19,333
[growling]

233
00:12:19,875 --> 00:12:21,667
Lloyd, it's a set up!

234
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:23,917
Don't foist your
excuses off on us.

235
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,250
We saw the whole
thing on-screen!

236
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:28,375
Bullying isn't tolerated.

237
00:12:28,458 --> 00:12:30,583
It's disqualification
and immediate exile.

238
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:32,583
But we didn't, that's not--

239
00:12:32,667 --> 00:12:37,375
Security bots, escort the ninja
beyond the city gates!

240
00:12:37,458 --> 00:12:38,625
[security bots chittering]

241
00:12:39,042 --> 00:12:44,000
Halt! I invoke article 764!

242
00:12:44,083 --> 00:12:48,250
The Cavern Run?
No one's done that in eons.

243
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:51,333
I totally know the rule book
inside and out

244
00:12:51,417 --> 00:12:53,625
but for those who might not
have devoted

245
00:12:53,708 --> 00:12:57,417
the hours of patient study,
I definitely have,
please fill us in?

246
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,667
It is a trial of worthiness.

247
00:12:59,750 --> 00:13:02,542
Compete in a dangerous,
high-speed vehicle race

248
00:13:02,625 --> 00:13:05,292
through deadly caverns,
beat the clock,

249
00:13:05,375 --> 00:13:07,208
and get immunity from exile.

250
00:13:07,583 --> 00:13:11,000
A desperate race against
the odds? Pure drama!

251
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:12,708
Stang-zoot, let's do it!

252
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:15,083
But it's. But, uh...

253
00:13:15,167 --> 00:13:16,500
Come on, Uncle Bleckt,

254
00:13:16,583 --> 00:13:18,958
you love old-school
traditional rules.

255
00:13:19,042 --> 00:13:20,750
This is your jam!

256
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:26,792
[sighs] I cannot deny the
legitimacy of article 764.

257
00:13:27,542 --> 00:13:30,083
Yes! We race tonight.

258
00:13:30,167 --> 00:13:32,792
I knew my games would
be the sweetest ever.

259
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,042
Sounds like we need a vehicle.

260
00:13:39,125 --> 00:13:41,500
One problem,
we don't have a vehicle.

261
00:13:41,583 --> 00:13:45,708
I'd let you use mine,
but it got trashed
on our way up here.

262
00:13:45,792 --> 00:13:48,083
Bleckt told me they dumped
it in their junkyard.

263
00:13:48,167 --> 00:13:50,750
[laughs] Thanks, Bleckt.

264
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:53,083
There's a junkyard up here?

265
00:13:53,167 --> 00:13:55,250
That might be
exactly what's needed

266
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:58,250
for someone with Elemental
Technology powers.

267
00:14:00,167 --> 00:14:02,292
[footsteps slapping]

268
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:06,625
[Kai] Riyu, we're putting
all our hope in you. Please!

269
00:14:06,708 --> 00:14:09,083
[Riyu whimpers]

270
00:14:09,167 --> 00:14:13,417
-[weapons whooshing]
-[footsteps tapping]

271
00:14:14,708 --> 00:14:16,792
[Riyu whimpers]

272
00:14:16,875 --> 00:14:19,875
[crowd chattering]

273
00:14:22,958 --> 00:14:25,042
Still don't have any wheels?

274
00:14:25,125 --> 00:14:27,042
You gonna beat the
Cavern Run on foot?

275
00:14:27,125 --> 00:14:29,875
[engine revving]

276
00:14:29,958 --> 00:14:33,833
-[engine roaring]
-[tires screeching]

277
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:40,083
[crowd cheering]

278
00:14:40,917 --> 00:14:43,417
[bold music]

279
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,042
Whoa!

280
00:14:47,875 --> 00:14:49,750
What were you saying, Cinder?

281
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:53,042
[crowd cheering]

282
00:14:53,125 --> 00:14:55,792
Arin, all eyes will
be on the race,

283
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:57,458
including theirs.

284
00:15:01,292 --> 00:15:03,917
So it's a good time
for a certain detective

285
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,833
to do some detectiving.

286
00:15:06,917 --> 00:15:08,917
I know that's not a word,
but it sounded right
in the moment.

287
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,583
Detective-away.

288
00:15:15,417 --> 00:15:17,792
Racers, to your vehicle!

289
00:15:19,125 --> 00:15:21,250
[engine revving]

290
00:15:24,083 --> 00:15:27,667
The ninja will be
racing the clock, right?

291
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:29,958
Well, meet the clock!

292
00:15:33,917 --> 00:15:35,250
The Pace Dragon!

293
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,958
That racing stripe? My addition.

294
00:15:37,958 --> 00:15:39,792
The Pace Dragon
will fly the course

295
00:15:39,875 --> 00:15:41,917
at the exact rate
needed to win the race.

296
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,208
If the ninja beat the
Pace Dragon, victory!

297
00:15:45,292 --> 00:15:47,583
Zero-percent exile!

298
00:15:47,667 --> 00:15:49,542
High stakes, Lloyd.

299
00:15:49,625 --> 00:15:51,750
Win this, the ninja
are still in the games.

300
00:15:51,833 --> 00:15:53,292
Lose, you're out.

301
00:15:53,375 --> 00:15:54,958
Do you have the
leadership skills

302
00:15:55,042 --> 00:15:57,583
to get your team across
the finish line in time?

303
00:15:57,667 --> 00:15:59,458
[Lloyd] Guess we'll find out.

304
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:02,542
Yes, yes, we will!

305
00:16:02,625 --> 00:16:05,500
Pure drama. Stang-zoot!

306
00:16:05,583 --> 00:16:08,833
[crowd cheering]

307
00:16:08,917 --> 00:16:12,667
Three, two, one. Go, go, go!

308
00:16:12,750 --> 00:16:16,333
-[engine roaring]
-[crowd cheering]

309
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:21,500
Woo-hoo.

310
00:16:21,583 --> 00:16:24,458
[spirited music]

311
00:16:28,958 --> 00:16:32,167
-[tires squealing]
-[engine roaring]

312
00:16:36,875 --> 00:16:39,708
Bye-bye, buddy.
See you at the finish line.

313
00:16:43,583 --> 00:16:45,750
[tense music]

314
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:48,458
[rattling]

315
00:16:51,625 --> 00:16:54,333
-Riyu?
-[Riyu grumbles]

316
00:16:54,417 --> 00:16:58,125
I was wondering where you were.
So you're investigating too?

317
00:16:58,208 --> 00:16:59,208
[Riyu chitters]

318
00:17:04,833 --> 00:17:07,875
[footsteps tapping]

319
00:17:07,958 --> 00:17:10,375
[door swishing]

320
00:17:10,458 --> 00:17:13,208
Okay, I'm searching for
anything that connects Ras

321
00:17:13,292 --> 00:17:15,917
to what happened with the
Matriarch or the attacker bots.

322
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,750
-[Kai] Can you hear me?
-[Riyu grumbles]

323
00:17:17,833 --> 00:17:19,833
Well, what is it?
You hear something?

324
00:17:19,917 --> 00:17:20,917
[Kai] It's Riyu.

325
00:17:21,792 --> 00:17:23,125
[Riyu rumbling]

326
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,833
I don't hear anything,
buddy.

327
00:17:24,917 --> 00:17:25,917
[Kai] Are you there, boy?

328
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:31,042
Um, okay, I guess you're
working on your own lead.

329
00:17:31,125 --> 00:17:33,417
[wooden tapping]

330
00:17:38,792 --> 00:17:42,417
Sora was right.
Frak is working for Ras.

331
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:45,083
[gasps] Doesn't he know
the guy is pure evil?

332
00:17:45,833 --> 00:17:47,750
Is Frak evil now too?

333
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:51,208
-[Riyu sniffing]
-[wooden tapping]

334
00:17:57,583 --> 00:17:58,792
[Riyu grumbles]

335
00:17:58,875 --> 00:18:00,750
[Kai] Riyu. I hear you, buddy!

336
00:18:00,833 --> 00:18:02,750
Ah, it's like you're right
next to me all of a sudden

337
00:18:02,833 --> 00:18:04,500
[Riyu whining]

338
00:18:05,625 --> 00:18:09,292
Riyu, what's going on?
Are you talking to a stone?

339
00:18:09,375 --> 00:18:12,542
'Cause, no judgment,
but that's kind of weird.

340
00:18:12,625 --> 00:18:14,375
[Riyu chittering]

341
00:18:14,458 --> 00:18:16,500
[Kai] What? Is someone with you?

342
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:17,917
I can only hear you.

343
00:18:20,125 --> 00:18:22,417
I don't get it.
It's just a stone.

344
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:25,708
I've never seen one glow
like that before though.

345
00:18:25,792 --> 00:18:27,000
What's it made of?

346
00:18:28,917 --> 00:18:30,042
[Riyu growling]

347
00:18:30,125 --> 00:18:32,500
[tense music]

348
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:36,000
[engine roaring]

349
00:18:36,083 --> 00:18:37,667
[Sora] You know,
they had me worried,

350
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:39,542
but this race is a breeze.

351
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:42,500
We are so far ahead
of that Pace Dragon.

352
00:18:42,583 --> 00:18:45,958
And according to this, we're
heading into the Green Zone.

353
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:47,042
Huh, sounds pleasant.

354
00:18:48,708 --> 00:18:50,917
[engine roaring]

355
00:18:52,792 --> 00:18:57,292
-[goo squelching]
-[tires squealing]

356
00:18:57,375 --> 00:18:59,917
Huh? Wait, toxic goo?

357
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Not pleasant. Way not pleasant.

358
00:19:02,083 --> 00:19:05,000
-[engine roaring]
-[dramatic music]

359
00:19:05,708 --> 00:19:10,500
Arin and his pet dragon.
Just like I suspected.

360
00:19:10,958 --> 00:19:14,792
Did your master, Lloyd,
set you up for this?

361
00:19:14,875 --> 00:19:16,667
Sending in one of
the youngest ninja,

362
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:19,708
and the only one without
an elemental power,

363
00:19:19,792 --> 00:19:21,667
into enemy territory

364
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:25,875
seems like Lloyd's
brand of leadership.

365
00:19:25,958 --> 00:19:27,958
I didn't need powers
to take you out

366
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,833
at the Ritual of the Blood Moon.

367
00:19:31,167 --> 00:19:36,042
[laughs] She really never
told you. You didn't hit me.

368
00:19:36,125 --> 00:19:38,417
Your little friend
used her tech abilities

369
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,500
to power the object
that struck me.

370
00:19:41,583 --> 00:19:45,542
No, I did it! Sora would've
told me if I didn't.

371
00:19:46,458 --> 00:19:49,958
[Kai] Riyu, what's going on?
Is... Is something happening?

372
00:19:50,042 --> 00:19:51,958
I can't hear you.

373
00:19:52,042 --> 00:19:54,583
Sora is hiding
the truth from you.

374
00:19:55,417 --> 00:19:59,208
Yet another lie from
your so-called teammates.

375
00:19:59,292 --> 00:20:02,375
Covering up for their inability
to train you, perhaps?

376
00:20:02,458 --> 00:20:04,208
I get all the training I need.

377
00:20:04,958 --> 00:20:07,750
Arin, you know that's not true.

378
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:11,542
The cycle of mastery eludes you.

379
00:20:11,625 --> 00:20:14,167
You obviously have potential.

380
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:18,958
If Lloyd Garmadon is incapable
of unleashing that potential...

381
00:20:19,042 --> 00:20:23,292
[sighs] ...perhaps you
need another master.

382
00:20:23,375 --> 00:20:25,792
One who sees you more clearly.

383
00:20:25,875 --> 00:20:27,417
Who? You?

384
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,083
I'd never join you.

385
00:20:29,875 --> 00:20:32,125
Your friend Frak
doesn't have an issue

386
00:20:32,208 --> 00:20:33,833
with being on my side.

387
00:20:33,917 --> 00:20:36,875
He must not know
how evil you are!

388
00:20:36,958 --> 00:20:39,625
Is it evil to want
to reverse the Merge?

389
00:20:41,208 --> 00:20:43,875
Wait, you wanna what?

390
00:20:43,958 --> 00:20:45,458
[Riyu grumbles]

391
00:20:45,542 --> 00:20:47,417
-[engine roaring]
-[tires squealing]

392
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:48,750
[Sora] Hold tight.

393
00:20:48,833 --> 00:20:51,583
[dramatic music]

394
00:20:52,542 --> 00:20:54,250
[goo squelching]

395
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:57,208
-[engine roaring]
-[tires squealing]

396
00:21:01,167 --> 00:21:02,667
[Lloyd] Sora, up front!

397
00:21:04,375 --> 00:21:05,708
[Sora] Oh, no!

398
00:21:05,792 --> 00:21:08,000
You speak of evil.

399
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:13,000
The Merge, that was
truly an act of evil.

400
00:21:13,083 --> 00:21:18,583
And since the Merge is what
took your parents away from you,

401
00:21:18,667 --> 00:21:20,500
I'm surprised you'd ever side

402
00:21:20,583 --> 00:21:23,417
with the students of the
very person that caused it.

403
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:24,542
[Arin] What?

404
00:21:25,792 --> 00:21:27,667
You don't know?

405
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:31,792
Your ninja's beloved
mentor, Master Wu.

406
00:21:31,875 --> 00:21:33,667
If it wasn't for him,

407
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:36,542
your parents never
would have been lost.

408
00:21:36,625 --> 00:21:38,458
What are you talking about?

409
00:21:38,542 --> 00:21:43,458
The Merge was
caused by Master Wu.

410
00:21:43,542 --> 00:21:44,958
[dramatic music]

411
00:21:45,042 --> 00:21:46,708
[closing theme music plays]

